\begin{align*}
\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \left( \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 9 \end{pmatrix} \right) &= 0 \\
\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} x - 2 \\ y - 9 \end{pmatrix} &= 0 \\
3(x - 2) + 7(y - 9) &= 0 \\
3x - 6 + 7y - 63 &= 0 \\
3x + 7y &= 69 \\
7y &= -3x + 69 \\
y &= -\frac{3}{7}x + \frac{69}{7}
\end{align*}

So, the ordered pair $(m,b)$ is $\boxed{\left(-\frac{3}{7}, \frac{69}{7}\right)}$.

