In a given cube, all eight vertices are tangent to a sphere with radius $r$. Three mutually perpendicular planes, each of which contains four of the vertices of the cube, are also tangent to three spheres, each with radius $R$. All four spheres are externally tangent to a fifth sphere with radius $s$. Find the relationship between the radii $r$, $R$, and $s$.

