solution:
To simplify $\sqrt[3]{24} + \sqrt[3]{54}$, we can factor out the perfect cubes from each term:
   \begin{align*}
   \sqrt[3]{24} + \sqrt[3]{54} &= \sqrt[3]{8 \cdot 3} + \sqrt[3]{27 \cdot 2} \\
   &= \sqrt[3]{2^3 \cdot 3} + \sqrt[3]{3^3 \cdot 2} \\
   &= 2\sqrt[3]{3} + 3\sqrt[3]{2}
   \end{align*}

Now we can add the two terms together:
\[ 2\sqrt[3]{3} + 3\sqrt[3]{2} = \boxed{2\sqrt[3]{3} + 3\sqrt[3]{2}} \]

